 claim. All 43 V20-O-R methods, eight table declarations, fixed anchor broker
 and policy bytes are preserved. Separate native review and execution remain
 required for this source candidate.
+
+
+### V20-O-R-I2 seals every membership touching the limited issuer
+
+V20-O-R-I included the issuer's role identity in the catalog, while its
+membership selection covered only actors and owners. An unrelated SET-only
+grant to the issuer would escape that selection. V20-O-R-I2 includes the
+issuer's exact OID in the same incident membership selection as actors and
+owners. The bootstrap grantor identity stays pinned without collecting all
+bootstrap memberships. The independent fixture verifier checks exactly the
+eight expected creator grants across both scopes and rejects extra issuer
+edges before sealing. The no-issuer profile still expects zero memberships.
+
+The focused case adds a rollback-only unrelated SET-only grant to the issuer.
+It observes the exact grant and effective SET authority before checking the
+reader denial under the held catalog. A fresh actual reader then retrieves
+the original bytes after rollback, with no retained grant or changed rows.
+The issuer authentication logic and all 43 V20-O-R methods are unchanged.
+This correction is source-only pending independent native verification.
